{
  "text": " 22% of women travelling alone at night pretend to be on a phone call. The national emergency response time is over 18 minutes. Over half of commuting women face harassment and 52% of them decline the job or college opportunities because of unsafe routes. When danger appears 95% of the time it is already someone known making a visible panic button impossible to press. Existing panic apps only trigger after an assault begins. Pukar activates 90 seconds before any escalation and turning the fake call she is already making into an active responsive 2 way conversation. She starts Pukar before entering any isolated street. The screen shows an ordinary incoming call as she speaks and AI persona replies naturally in English. When she says a very simple everyday sentence like no I already told mom I will eat at home. Pukar silently extracts the intent, dispatches her life GPS trade to trusted contacts and keeps the talking without missing a key. Under the hood safety is never left to single points of failure. The audio streams and web sockets to a cloud relay with 1.2 second latency budget. If network connectivity drops and on device local phrase match it triggers the alert independently. Privacy is strictly bounded. Pukar never records idle background audio, stores the zero voice transcripts and clears the live GPS tokens automatically the moment commute concludes. Rollout begins with 34,000 women admitted across Delhi University and Delhi colleges. Optimized streaming STT and TTS keep the TRA infrastructure cost under 13N rupees per 20 minute protected commute. Pukar the call she was already pretending to make made real with the alarm hidden inside.",
